WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.590
I am going to throw to an interview right now

2
00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:05.280
with a guest.

3
00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.280
Some people would call picture perfect.

4
00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.550
She's a photographer, Gillian Laub.

5
00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:12.820
What I love about this conversation is,

6
00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:17.570
it's a lot of political views can come under one roof.

7
00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:19.420
And how do we deal with that?

8
00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:21.210
How do we find our common ground?

9
00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:22.920
How do we listen to each other?

10
00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.790
How do we accept each other?

11
00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:26.710
How do we have different viewpoints?

12
00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:28.490
All in one home.

13
00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:32.840
This is what's happening in our world, let alone country,

14
00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:34.330
and we find our way

15
00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:37.730
and Gillian documented her family's way.

16
00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:40.380
And I can't wait for you to take a look.

17
00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:44.990
Gillian, what gave you the idea to do this book?

18
00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:46.340
What was the inspiration? What was the spark?

19
00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:51.340
So, I have been photographing my family for over 20 years

20
00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:53.790 line:15%
and it was more of a personal project.

21
00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:56.150 line:15%
I have a very colorful family

22
00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:58.350 line:15%
with lots of characters in them.

23
00:00:58.350 --> 00:00:59.780 line:15%
You do.
So--

24
00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:01.400 line:15%
That's my grandfather on the cover.

25
00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:04.800 line:15%
I love this cover, I really do.

26
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.360
So it was really more of a personal project.

27
00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:11.293
And then in 2016,

28
00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:13.940
there was a rift in our family.

29
00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.090
And I, you know,

30
00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:20.210
I've always prided myself on having the closest family.

31
00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:21.950
And then in 2016,

32
00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:25.640
my parents became passionate Trump supporters.

33
00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:29.120
And like I do with all of my photography,

34
00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:33.510
I work, my work helps me work through, you know,

35
00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:35.410
what I'm going through personally.

36
00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:37.800
And I continued to photograph my family.

37
00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.330
And then I realized

38
00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:42.250
that my family was really just a microcosm

39
00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:45.720
of what so many families in America were going through.

40
00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.150
And that's when I decided to make it a book.

41
00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:50.700
I mean, I just think there's so much great stuff going on

42
00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:53.410
in this photograph, politics aside,

43
00:01:53.410 --> 00:01:55.260
is your, is that, is that your mom?

44
00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:56.093
So that's my mom.

45
00:01:56.093 --> 00:01:56.930
Is she meditating?

46
00:01:56.930 --> 00:02:01.930
She was at the end of a yoga class and she's in Shavasana.

47
00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:03.270
So she is meditating.

48
00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:05.330
Perfect, okay, in the next photograph,

49
00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:08.010
may I say, yeah, I love this one.

50
00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:09.870
And who is this member of your family?

51
00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:11.470
Oh, this is my cousin Violet.

52
00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:14.030
And she's the family activist.

53
00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:17.470
Yeah and completely in a 180,

54
00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:21.630
we've got the AOC, the Elizabeth Warren, the Obama.

55
00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:24.343
That must be fun and interesting at the dinner table.

56
00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:27.940
So she's a high school student here.

57
00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:31.400
And when I made this portrait of her in her bedroom,

58
00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:33.940
I asked her, you know, how do you feel?

59
00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:36.300
Are you, you know, are you embarrassed?

60
00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:39.490
Are you ashamed that you're going to be in a book with,

61
00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:42.120
you know, your Trump supporting loving family?

62
00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:45.960
And she looked at me and she's like, why, why would I be?

63
00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:49.530
And she said, Gillian, like, listen,

64
00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:50.930
listen to what they have to say.

65
00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:52.510
You know, they have an opinion too.

66
00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:56.270
And to me, that was so inspiring.

67
00:02:56.270 --> 00:03:00.090
So, I love, I love this picture because she represents that.

68
00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:02.830
Can we go to the next photograph?

69
00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:05.050
Okay, there you go.

70
00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:06.700
That, that pretty much says it all.

71
00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:09.340
What do you think when you look at this photograph?

72
00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:10.700
Let alone, when you took it.

73
00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:12.030
This gives me,

74
00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:13.070
I love this

75
00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:16.450
because this is my mom with her best friend, Bonnie,

76
00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:19.040
who is like a second mom to me.

77
00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:20.040
And to me,

78
00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.640
this is really is just about the power of friendship.

79
00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:26.200
And they had some tough moments

80
00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:28.090
in the past four years,

81
00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:31.870
but they just love each other so much

82
00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:33.190
and to them,

83
00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:35.850
that was way more important than anything else.

84
00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:37.310
I love that.

85
00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:38.410
Yeah
So thank you

86
00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:40.967
for your keen eye Gillian.
Thank you.

87
00:03:40.967 --> 00:03:42.158
Gillian Laub

88
00:03:42.158 --> 00:03:43.160
(audience clapping)

89
00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:46.250
I embrace that we all have our differences

90
00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:49.610
and I think discussing it or knowing when to walk away,

91
00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:51.250
whatever it is,

92
00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:55.440
to find our common ground is so much of my life's mission.

93
00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:57.990
So 'Family Matters', Gillian's book

94
00:03:57.990 --> 00:04:00.810
an exhibition at the International Center of Photography,

95
00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:02.993
which is by the way, the big leagues.

96
00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:05.911
And please check it out.

97
00:04:05.911 --> 00:04:10.911
(closing music)

